# Japanese theorem — the incenters of the two triangles cut off by a diagonal of a cyclic quadrilateral, taken for both diagonals, form a rectangle (source: Japanese temple geometry; Johnson)
A B C = triangle
O = circumcenter(A, B, C)
D = reflect(B, O)
I1 = incenter(A, B, C)
I2 = incenter(A, C, D)
I3 = incenter(A, B, D)
I4 = incenter(B, C, D)
prove perp(I1, I3, I3, I2)
